A second check lists the countries that have a national value and no forest weight in some year. Such a country would lose its flow. A national NAI of zero, as in Malta, is not a loss.

lapply(names(weight_sums), \(y) mutate(weight_sums[[y]], year = as.integer(y))) |&gt;
  bind_rows() |&gt;
  right_join(nai_filled |&gt; filter(year %in% years_report), by = c("geo", "year")) |&gt;
  filter((is.na(weight_sum) | weight_sum &lt;= 0) & value &gt; 0) |&gt;
  select(Year = year, Country = geo, `NAI (1000 m3)` = value) |&gt;
  show_table(digits = 0)

